WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.319 --> 00:00:10.030
Hello fellow travellers,

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:17.100
We launched Journey to the Microcosmos knowing
that there would be, y’know, some people

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:23.279
who would be interested in the magnificence
of this world that exists beyond our view

00:00:23.279 --> 00:00:29.140
and that some portion of those people would
like to enjoy that world with a more laid

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:32.800
back vibe than your average YouTube video.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:42.780
That feels like a fraction of a fraction of an audience so we were not expecting this level of response.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:47.940
Your comments, your thoughts, your support, it's been really special for us.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:53.460
For James and his cultures in Europe, for
me and Matt here in Missoula Montana.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:58.760
And for Deboki over on the east coast, writing
and fact checking, this process has been really

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:02.769
something special.

00:01:02.769 --> 00:01:07.050
Starting out, we planned to make a total of 30 episodes
of Journey to the Microcosmos.

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:14.980
We’re now on our way to episode 15 and no one on the team thinks that we’re half way done with

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:16.730
this anymore.

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:18.360
We want to keep going.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.240
We want more original music from Andrew Huang.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:28.640
We want better equipment so we can see more
and deeper at higher resolutions and framerates.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:35.280
We want more time and resources to get to
the bottom of the mysteries we’re most curious about.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:42.159
We also want to provide the folks that love
what we do with a little extra, and to get you involved.

00:01:42.159 --> 00:01:47.540
So, as you might have expected would eventually
happen, and as many of you have been asking

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:51.869
for, which is wonderful, we have a
Patreon now.

00:01:51.869 --> 00:01:53.900
Our Patreon only has one level.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:58.540
It’s $8 a month and it gets everyone the
same things:

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:05.020
First, you’ll be thanked in the credits
of all videos while you’re a Patreon.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:12.540
Second, once a month we’ll be sending you an hour-long, un-narrated video that will show off Andrew Huang's

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:16.370
full-length tracks and deeper cuts of our
footage.

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:23.420
And third, a weekly wallpaper...an image, as high resolution as we can get, of some of our favorite

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:29.980
microbes for you to use on your computer,
phone, or just print out and put on your

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:32.040
actual wall.

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:36.820
We know that, ultimately, what people want out of a Patreon is to support the channel,

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:39.110
not to make a bunch of extra work for us.

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:43.260
And that’s what we want to...and we want
to thank you.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:48.070
I’ve been making YouTube videos for a long
time, and I have never had a channel gather

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:55.130
such a diehard fanbase so fast. This has been really wonderful.

00:02:55.130 --> 00:03:01.780
Thank you for coming on this journey with us as we explore the unseen world that surrounds us.

